
phaser
-----------------------------------------------
A Phaser is a synchronization tool in Java used when multiple
 threads work in stages (phases) and must wait for each other after each stage.

It is like an advanced version of:

CountDownLatch
CyclicBarrier
------------------------------------------------
Very Simple Example
3 Students in Competition
They must complete:
Registration
Round 1
Round 2
Final Round
After each round:
Everyone waits until all finish, then next round starts.
That system = Phaser
-----------------------------------------------------
Why Name Phaser?
Because work happens in phases / steps.
Phase 1
Phase 2
Phase 3
---------------------------------------------------
Constructor
Basic
Phaser phaser = new Phaser(3);
Means:
3 participating threads.
----------------------------------------------------
Main Methods

arriveAndAwaitAdvance()
phaser.arriveAndAwaitAdvance();
Meaning:
I completed current phase
Wait for others
Then move next phase together

arrive()
phaser.arrive();
I finished phase, not waiting.

register()
phaser.register();
Add new participant dynamically.

arriveAndDeregister()
phaser.arriveAndDeregister();
Finish and leave phaser.

getPhase()
phaser.getPhase();
Current phase number.
--------------------------------------
Why Use Phaser?

When work has many rounds.

Examples:

Multi-step batch jobs
Multiplayer game rounds
Data processing stages
Testing pipelines
------------------------------------------
| Tool           | Use                               |
| -------------- | --------------------------------- |
| CountDownLatch | Wait once                         |
| CyclicBarrier  | Wait each round fixed threads     |
| Phaser         | Wait each round + dynamic threads |
